# component: pagination
# decisions: A11Y-23, DOC-1, DOC-2, VOI-1
# hunks:
#   A11Y-23: `PaginationLink` renders a real `<a>` wearing `buttonVariants({ variant, size })`
#     instead of `Button nativeButton={false} render={<a/>}`, which stamped `role="button"` on a
#     link. A pagination link navigates, so it keeps the link role; `aria-current="page"` stays.
#     (A pager whose controls change state rather than navigate renders buttons — `DataListPager`.)
#   VOI-1: upstream's lower-case `aria-label="pagination"` becomes "Pagination", overridable with
#     `label`, and the ellipsis's "More pages" is overridable with `morePagesLabel`.
#   Otherwise NO STYLING HUNK. `PaginationLink` wears the `Button` recipe, which already carries
#     this system's focus, cursor and disabled behaviour (Batch 2), so pagination inherits FOC-1,
#     FOC-5, FOC-6 and FRM-4 rather than restating them. A11Y-2: audited — every control is a
#     `Button` at `size="icon"` (32px) or `size="default"`, and `PaginationEllipsis` is
#     `aria-hidden` and not a control. `pagination.test.tsx` measures both.
#   cn: `import { cn } from "cn"` becomes `@vegastack/design` — our npm layer owns `cn` (DOC-2).
#   formatting: the repository formatter (prettier defaults: semicolons, trailing commas)
#               reflows the file, and `registry-stamp.mjs` writes the provenance header the
#               three-copy model needs (DOC-1); those hunks carry no decision of their own.
